WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.500
A question I get asked all the time is
"Luca how can they speak better and more

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.389
confidently and faster?" and the simple
reply is: in order to speak well, you have

00:00:09.389 --> 00:00:13.830
to speak you have to get into the habit
of speaking regularly. And there are

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:19.020
many ways, and many circumstances and many
people you can talk to, but one very

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.250
efficient thing that you can do - and you
can do it directly at your place if you

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.150
have an internet connection and a nice
computer - is simply to have a language

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.230
exchange. So what I'm going to do now is
I'm going to show you a few but

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.500
extremely important and efficient
things to keep in mind to have a

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.750
fantastic language change and remember
there's always a final super cool tip at

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:47.930
the end of the video, so stay here until
the end. If you want to create a great

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.739
sustainable efficient routine for
language exchange, the first step that

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:58.140
you have to do is make decisions. Take a
piece of paper and write down WHY you

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:03.629
want to do this. It has to be clear to
you and WHEN. Put a starting date and

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.890
tell yourself "from this moment on I'm
going to start taking language exchanges

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:13.979
every single week". Maybe you find
yourself in some parts of the world

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:18.030
where meeting people and talking to them
face-to-face is kind of problematic

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.979
especially if you're looking for foreigners
or maybe you do live in a cosmopolitan

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:26.400
city where there's a chance of meeting a
lot of people but you simply don't want

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.420
to and you want to be at the comfort of
your own place and talk through Skype or

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.060
through the Internet in general. So the
next thing you want to do is to find

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.110
platforms where you can find native
speakers to talk to, and as usual, the

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:45.479
internet offers a deluge, a wealth of
possibilities but here's the thing: the

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:49.439
problem is that there are so many
platforms that offer the service that

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:53.909
it's difficult to choose a good one so
make sure that you invest the time and

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:59.820
find one good platform that you like,
be it because it's user friendly, be it

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.030
because you like it visually, the
important thing is you find just one and

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:07.979
use that, and possibly move on
to another one oh and by the way in the

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:13.320
description box you will find a list of
platforms that I have used or that I

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:21.150
highly recommend. So now you have:
compelling reasons, a date of reference

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:26.040
and then on top of that you have found your
favorite platform. What is the next step?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.020
So the next step is to build a very cool
profile because that's what people are

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.620
going to take a look at and based on
that they're going to make a decision

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.640
whether they want to have a language
exchange with you or not. A good profile

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.410
has to be compelling, short, simple, 
possibly in two or three other languages

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:51.900
Remember: it's really important. So having
a good profile is fantastic but it's not

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.950
enough. People might contact you or
people might not contact you, so if

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.720
people don't contact you - which is
possible - you have to contact THEM, and in

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.070
that regard you have to send a very cool
message. I don't know if it has ever

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:08.400
happened to you that you were trying to
contact as many people as possible on

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.739
other platforms maybe and you created
the same stock message that you sent to

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:18.090
everybody. So, in that regard don't make
that mistake. What you should do is to

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:24.060
look into other people's profiles to
look for one or two details and then use

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.890
that as a hook, because that gives the
impression that you have actually read

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.450
the profile that you got interested in
that profile instead of sending the same

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.709
message to everyone remember the profile
building your own profile is important

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:42.209
but also sending people a compelling
message, a personal message is really

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:46.489
important to get into a cool connection.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:53.270
So imagine that you send this cool
message, the person replied and you're

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:57.050
finally going to have your language 
exchange. Now what do you want to do is

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.670
don't focus too much on the language, but
focus on communication, focus on

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:05.900
interaction, focus on cooperation. That's
what counts the most the first

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:11.360
impression is always the strongest and
the most important. So it's not about the

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.350
quantity of words, the cool expressions
that you use, the fact that you're using

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:22.300
the language but focus on speaking,
smiling, interacting, asking, being curious

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:27.590
when the person talks, listen attentively
that creates a very positive environment

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:32.510
and that is going to work wonders for
your language learning skills and his or

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:36.550
her language learning skills

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.720
Whatever happens, always make sure that
you record the conversation, this is

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.680
really important and it's easy to do
nowadays you can use a mobile phone

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.720
maybe your iPad, your computer, so whether
you have a conversation on the Internet

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.370
through Skype or other software programs
or you have an in real life, always make

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.810
sure that you have a recording device
with you. Remember recording the

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:04.040
information is really important because
later you can take a look at it you can

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.940
take a listen or again you can even see
it if you're recording video and that

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:12.320
will be really useful to further
memorize the information that is being

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.640
processed there. So here you have it: with
these six simple tips just get into a

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:20.240
language exchange, just jump into it
don't think about it too much and you

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.650
will see what an enormous difference it
can make it can be free, it can be

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:28.820
efficient, if you find the right language
partner you can do it on a weekly basis

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:33.200
maybe a couple of times a week - and if
you do it well and you find this good

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.520
environment, good positive environment of
cooperation, of stimulation of

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.750
inspiration, you will be able to do this
for a long time and it will work wonders

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.910
for your language
skills it will prepare you for real

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:52.860
conversations in real life. As always, I
have written an extensive article about

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:57.150
it and I read it out loud and I have
extra tips and video demonstrations

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:01.979
on the blog, so please click on the link
in the description box, head over the

00:06:01.979 --> 00:06:07.919
blog and let's have a very constructive
and cool cooperation to build our language

00:06:07.919 --> 00:06:14.370
skills in any language. So as usual, I
have one question and one cool tip. So

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.819
the question goes like this: have you
ever had a language exchange and what

00:06:17.819 --> 00:06:23.009
are your best strategies when it comes
to communicating, interacting for example

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:27.120
through Skype or through another
software program, how did that go what

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:32.400
did you learn, what about your failures and
victories, please share all your stories

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.409
in the comment section below, I will be
more than happy to reply and hopefully

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:42.120
we can have a constructive conversation
we can learn from one another. So, time

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.500
for one final extra tip. Always make
sure that when you talk, when you get

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.770
your point across whatever you're
talking about the person who's listening

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:55.710
to you takes notes and writes down and
provides the feedback at the end of your

00:06:55.710 --> 00:07:00.360
language exchange. In this way, you can
then take a look you can listen to the

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.830
recording and you can take a look at the
feedback that was given to you that was

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:09.389
that is written that you can actually
see and you can learn from it, so always

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:13.770
make sure that you go back to what you
did for the sake of learning because

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:17.610
when you take a look at it again without
having to speak because you're just

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:21.150
listening to the recording, you're
attacking the piece of information from

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:25.289
another angle, you're not stressed you
can just focus on learning and

00:07:25.289 --> 00:07:29.580
extracting the information that was
given to you while you were talking. This

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:35.580
always makes a huge difference and if
you can, maybe reduce the amount of

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.840
language exchanges that you do twice a
week but always make sure that you

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:45.599
absorb the information later by
listening 48 hours after each language

00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:58.669
exchange

